Average rate of disappearance of H_2 = \frac{\Delta[H_2]}{\Delta t}
Instantaneous rate of formation of NH&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt; = \frac{d[NH_3]}{dt}
Instantaneous rate of disappearance of N_2 = -\frac{d[N_2]}{dt}
Instantaneous rate of disappearance of H_2 = \frac{d[H_2]}{dt}
To equate the three rates, divide each rate by the coefficient of the corresponding substances in the balanced equation.
Average rate = +\frac{1}{2} \frac{\Delta[NH_3]}{\Delta t} = -\frac{\Delta[N_2]}{\Delta t} = -\frac{1}{3} \frac{\Delta[H_2]}{\Delta t}

Instantaneous rate = \frac{1}{2} \frac{d[NH_3]}{dt} = -\frac{d[N_2]}{dt} = -\frac{1}{3} \frac{d[H_2]}{dt}
